            <ArticleTitle>In-situ ethylenediamine-assisted synthesis of a magnetic iron-based metal-organic framework MIL-53(Fe) for visible light photocatalysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-37</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0021-9797(17)30069-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jcis.2017.01.060</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel magnetic MIL-53(Fe) photocatalyst (MAG-MIL) has been synthesized by an in-situ ethylenediamine (EDA)-assisted solvothermal method. The well dispersed γ-Fe2O3 nanoparticles embedded in the MAG-MIL framework contribute to a red shift of the light absorption edge as well as the superparamagnetism characteristic.</AbstractText>
